# The dense page word (--no-page-masks): the shift-xor, written under an
# enable, writes its old value back where the enable is low.
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MOD < %t/mod.log
# MOD: pages Leaf: p 3, 3 registers, 181 bits; page RAMs
# Without --page nothing pages.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/plain --static Leaf > %t/plain.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAIN < %t/plain/foldsim_sim.sv
# ONE: pages Leaf: p 1, 4 registers, 189 bits (196 in 9-bit bytes, 1 enables); page RAMs 4 rows x 198 bits in 1 columns, 3 ports, block; kept 0 registers, 0 bits
# CHAIN: pages Leaf: p 2, 3 registers, 181 bits (187 in 9-bit bytes, 1 enables); page RAMs 4 rows x 99 bits in 2 columns, 2 ports, block; kept 1 registers, 8 bits
# CHAIN: pages Leaf_copy1: p 2,
# NEST: pages Leaf: p 4, 3 registers, 181 bits (187 in 9-bit bytes, 1 enables); page RAMs 16 rows x 54 bits in 1 columns, 1 ports, block; kept 1 registers, 8 bits; state passes 4 x 4 = 16
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH 196 cycles
# PLAIN-NOT: fetch3
